<title>CROATIA: Croatia M1 money supply down, M4 up in September.</title>
<headline>Croatia M1 money supply down, M4 up in September.</headline>
<dateline>ZAGREB 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Croatia issued the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> CROATIA MONETARY AGGREGATES   SEPTEMBER     AUGUST    SEPT '95</p>
<p> Reserve money (million HRK)    7,881.6     7,995.8     6,437.3</p>
<p> M1 money supply		   10,326.4    10,454.1     8,363.5</p>
<p> -Currency outside banks	  3,918.8     4,069.4     3,094.0</p>
<p> Broadest money M4		 33,237.6    32,660.5    22,830.2</p>
<p>NOTE -- September reserve money shrank 1.43 percent and M1 1.22 percent from August. Total liquid assets (broadest money) M4 rose 1.77 percent on a monthly level.</p>
<p>-- Zagreb Newsroom, 385-1-4557075</p>
</text>
